We introduced stars, but we also kept ctx.clearRect and fillRect for background; added duplicate clearRect. Need to fix rendering logic: we should not clear twice; we should fill background and stars, then draw ship, meteors, etc. Probably we need to adjust: remove the second clearRect and ensure drawing order.

Better: replace the segment where we render; currently after edit, we have:

```
    // Render
    // Dark space background
    ctx.fillStyle = '#000010';
    ctx.fillRect(0, 0, canvas.width, canvas.height);
    // Update and draw stars
    ctx.fillStyle = 'white';
    for (const s of stars) {
      s.y += s.speed;
...
